<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">12 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 12 November, from 954 to 1970.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-i" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lothair-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/954">954 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,072 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lothair is crowned king of West Francia at Reims</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The 13-year-old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-i">Lothair</a>, whose reign as king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-francia">West Francia</a> had begun on 10 September, was crowned at the Abbey of Saint-Remi in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reims">Reims</a>. The penultimate Carolingian king of West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francia">Francia</a>, he ruled until his death in 986.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-francia">West Francia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1028 CE <span class="tih-ago">998 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Zoe becomes Byzantine empress with Romanos III</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">As her father Constantine VIII lay dying, Zoe was married to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanos-iii-argyros">Romanos III</a>, who became emperor. She went on to share the throne with three husbands, an adopted son and her sister Theodora.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1330">1330 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">696 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Basarab I's Wallachians nearly annihilate the Hungarian army at Posada</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-posada">Battle of Posada</a>, fought between 9 and 12 November, Wallachians under the voivode <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basarab-i">Basarab I</a> ambushed and nearly annihilated the invading army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-hungary">Charles I of Hungary</a>, ending Hungarian suzerainty in Wallachia.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-posada">Battle of Posada</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1859">1859 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">167 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jules Léotard performs the first flying trapeze act</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the Cirque Napoléon in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, Jules Léotard swung between trapezes in the first flying trapeze act. The close-fitting garment he wore still bears his name.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1912">1912 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">114 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Searchers find the tent of Scott's polar party</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A search party found the snow-covered tent containing the bodies of Robert Falcon Scott and two companions, eight months after their deaths returning from the South Pole. Scott's diary told their story.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1918">1918 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Austria is proclaimed a republic</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A day after Emperor Charles I renounced participation in state affairs, the provisional national assembly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> proclaimed the Republic of German-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> rule there, dating from 1278, was over.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1920">1920 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">106 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Italy and Yugoslavia settle their border in the Treaty of Rapallo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes">Slovenes</a> signed the Treaty of Rapallo, settling their post-war border. Italy received Istria, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zadar">Zara</a> and several islands, the rest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a> went to the Yugoslav kingdom, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rijeka">Fiume</a> became a free state.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-rapallo-1920">Treaty of Rapallo (1920)</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1970">1970 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">56 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Bhola cyclone devastates East Pakistan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A cyclone and storm surge struck the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-pakistan">East Pakistan</a>, killing perhaps 300,000 to 500,000 people. Anger at the government's response fed the movement that led to Bangladesh's independence.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 12 November <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jeanne-mance"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jeanne-mance.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jeanne Mance</span><span class="tp">1606–1673</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/diego-luis-de-san-vitores"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/diego-luis-de-san-vitores.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Diego Luis de San Vitores</span><span class="tp">1627–1672</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francis-nicholson"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Francis Nicholson</span><span class="tp">1655–1728</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/edward-vernon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/edward-vernon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Edward Vernon</span><span class="tp">1684–1757</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gerhard-von-scharnhorst"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gerhard-von-scharnhorst.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gerhard von Scharnhorst</span><span class="tp">1755–1813</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/piet-retief"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/piet-retief.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Piet Retief</span><span class="tp">1780–1838</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sun-yat-sen"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sun-yat-sen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sun Yat-sen</span><span class="tp">1866–1925</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/benjamin-mkapa"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/benjamin-mkapa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Benjamin Mkapa</span><span class="tp">1938–2020</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 12 November <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/cnut-the-great"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cnut-the-great.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Cnut the Great</span><span class="tp">c. 990–1035</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/canute-vi-of-denmark"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/canute-vi-of-denmark.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Canute VI of Denmark</span><span class="tp">1163–1202</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-henry-margrave-of-moravia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-henry-margrave-of-moravia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John Henry, Margrave of Moravia</span><span class="tp">1322–1375</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/liu-shaoqi"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/liu-shaoqi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Liu Shaoqi</span><span class="tp">1898–1969</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
